@* Batch R requirements 3(a)/4/5: the verse/passage popover section --
   compact by default (the SAME single-verse-or-passage text the popover
   already showed pre-Batch-R), with an expand affordance that grows the
   popover and turns this section into a SCROLLABLE mini-reader of the
   WHOLE chapter, auto-scrolled to the focal verse/passage with a calm
   highlight, and place-name hover -> map marker blink.

   Batch F2, 6-ARCH ("reuse the bits that we have... if you can't, refactor
   for composability"): the expand/mini-reader MECHANISM itself now lives in
   MiniReaderExpand.razor (client/Components/), shared with every OTHER
   passage entry in the popover platform (PassageList.razor: cross-
   references, THE SCRIPTURES, place est/dest). This file is now a thin
   wrapper supplying the ONE thing genuinely specific to the focal-verse
   section -- its own compact rendering (bare text, no ref label; the
   popover's own title already IS the ref, "the subject, not context" per
   requirement 6) -- and the empty TestIdSuffix, which reproduces this
   section's own pre-existing testids (popover-verse-expand/-reader/
   -reader-verse-{n}) byte for byte. VerseTextSectionProvider (Explore/
   PopoverSectionProviders.cs) is still the ONLY thing that constructs this
   component.

   Batch M-D4 ("the recursive reader," decision 3 "name links everywhere...
   render wherever verse text renders"): this compact preview was, before
   this batch, the ONE place verse text rendered with NO in-text mention
   links at all -- CompactText a bare, unscanned string (VerseNode.Detail's
   own plain .Text, or PassageNode's own pre-known concatenation), neither
   of which carries the Places/Persons PlaceMentions.Scan needs. FocalVerses
   (new) is VerseTextSectionProvider's own fail-soft ENHANCEMENT: the SAME
   focal verse range, resolved instead via `GET /api/chapter/{cref}` (the
   wire data need decision 3 anticipates -- "if any surface's data path
   lacks spans, EXTEND that fetch's DTO... never a parallel path" -- no
   server change, no graph-types touch: the chapter endpoint already carries
   Places/Persons per verse, VerseTextSectionProvider was simply the one
   caller that never asked for it), rendered per-verse through
   MentionText.razor -- the SAME component VerseLine.razor uses, no third
   copy of the scan-and-render loop. CompactText survives as the FALLBACK:
   whenever the chapter fetch fails (fail-soft try/catch at section resolve,
   the house pattern), FocalVerses is empty and this falls straight back to
   the exact plain-text rendering this section always had -- a genuine
   network-reliability regression (PassageNode's own text used to be
   zero-fetch, always-available; now it depends on a fetch that COULD fail)
   is deliberately never introduced. No verse-num, no xref superscript here
   -- "bare text, no ref label" is unchanged (the popover's own title
   already IS the ref); a superscript would also be pure noise immediately
   above the unconditional, inline cross-references section one hop below
   it -- see this batch's own report for the fuller "where applicable"
   scoping call. *@
@using BibleAtlas.Client.Explore

<div class="popover-verse-section">
    <MiniReaderExpand Book="@Book" Chapter="@Chapter" FocalFromVerse="@FocalFromVerse" FocalToVerse="@FocalToVerse" OnExplore="OnExplore">
        <CompactContent>
            <p class="popover-verse-text">
                @if (FocalVerses.Count > 0)
                {
                    @foreach (var v in FocalVerses)
                    {
                        <MentionText Text="@v.Text" Places="@v.Places" Persons="@v.Persons" Verse="@v.Verse"
                                     ClassPrefix="popover-verse-mention" OnExplore="OnExplore" /><text> </text>
                    }
                }
                else
                {
                    @CompactText
                }
            </p>
        </CompactContent>
    </MiniReaderExpand>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Book { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public int Chapter { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public int FocalFromVerse { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public int FocalToVerse { get; set; }
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string CompactText { get; set; } = default!;

    // Batch M-D4: the SAME focal range as CompactText, with real per-verse
    // Places/Persons -- empty (never null) whenever VerseTextSectionProvider's
    // own chapter fetch failed, in which case the markup above falls back
    // to CompactText's plain string. See this file's own header comment.
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyList<VerseOut> FocalVerses { get; set; } = Array.Empty<VerseOut>();

    // M-D3/U5: forwarded straight through to MiniReaderExpand -- this
    // component has no popover-stack access of its own (VerseTextSectionProvider,
    // PopoverSectionProviders.cs, is the one place a real ctx.PushAsync exists).
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback<IExplorable> OnExplore { get; set; }
}
